Use BakaSU SELinux callbacks with the SUSFS 2.3.0 kernel patch.

Apply after 50_add_susfs_in_gki-android14-6.1.patch, only for BakaSU
(including the SukiSU option redirected to BakaSU). BakaSU exports
my_write_context, my_write_access and my_setprocattr when SUSFS manual
hooks are detected, but does not provide the legacy fake_state object.
The callbacks retain the backup-policy checks and SELinux permissions.

Reference: Baka-SU/BakaSU@548d1dda, kernel/feature/selinux_hide.c

